  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}=0,\\,y(-2)=0,\\,y(2)-4{y}^{\u2032}(2)=0,\\,-2\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\nFind the solution to this boundary value problem in terms of an arbitrary constant $A.$\n\nThe solution is $y=A\\,\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}$).$",
  "worked_solution": "To solve the homogeneous boundary value problem, we first find the general solution and then determine the values of the arbitrary constants that fit the boundary conditions.\n\nWe have the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}(x)=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation twice, we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=A.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition $y(-2)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n-2A+B=0\\,\u21d2\\,B=2A.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\ny=Ax+2A=A(x+2).\n$$\n\nApplying the condition $y(2)-4{y}^{\u2032}(2)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n4A-4A=0\n$$\n\nwhich is automatically satisfied for any $A.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the BVP is $y=A\\cdot (x+2),$ where $A$ is arbitrary.",
